        "question": "Which unsigned types does this skill add?",
        "answer": "It adds PyTorch support for uint16, uint32, and uint64 through barebones unsigned dispatch types."
      },
      {
        "question": "Does this include uint8?",
        "answer": "No. PyTorch represents uint8 as kByte, which belongs to the existing integral type group."
      },
      {
        "question": "Can it update old dispatch macros?",
        "answer": "No. Convert old macros to AT_DISPATCH_V2 first, then apply the unsigned type update."
      },
      {
        "question": "Which update method should I choose?",
        "answer": "Use AT_INTEGRAL_TYPES_V2 when replacing an integral group. Otherwise, add the barebones unsigned group explicitly."
      },
